{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7c0a0b4-1a4e-4f6a-9d3d-2a1c3f6e8a11",
    "name": "Dwara API - Auth Controller",
    "description": "Focused Postman tests for AuthController only: POST /auth/register (signup), POST /auth/login and GET /auth/me.\n\nSetup:\n- Set the `baseUrl` collection variable if the API is not on http://localhost:8080.\n- Set `password` if you want a different test password (default: hunter2).\n- `userEmail`, `userId` and `jwt` are populated automatically by the requests; run the folder top to bottom with the Collection Runner.\n- Each run registers one new account with a unique generated email, so repeated runs do not collide.\n\nNote on status codes: this API wraps business failures in a 200 response with `success: false` (see ResponseObject), so the register/login tests assert on the `success` flag and `message` rather than on HTTP status.\n\nKnown backend defect surfaced by `Me - no token`: `/auth/**` is permitAll in SecurityConfig, so a request with no (or an invalid) JWT reaches the controller with a null principal and `userRepository.findById(null)` fails, giving a 500 and Spring's default error body instead of the 401 the app expects. That assertion is intentionally kept at the documented contract; it fails until the controller guards a null `userId`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "AuthController endpoints. Run in order: register -> duplicate register -> login -> me.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register (signup)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Fresh unique email on every run so the collection is repeatable.",
                  "const suffix = Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userEmail', `postman.${suffix}@example.com`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Registration succeeded', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Registered successfully.');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Payload carries the new user', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.userId).to.match(/^[0-9a-fA-F-]{36}$/);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('userEmail'));",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.name).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('No password material is returned', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(JSON.stringify(body)).to.not.include('passwordHash');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.data.userId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman User\",\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"rawPassword\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a USER account (role is forced server-side). Saves `userId` for later assertions."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register - duplicate email",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Duplicate email is rejected in the body', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(false);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('User already exists.');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.eql(null);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman User\",\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"rawPassword\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-registering the email created by the previous request. Business failure is reported with HTTP 200 and success:false."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Login succeeded', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Login successful.');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('JWT is returned', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.jwt).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.jwt.split('.')).to.have.lengthOf(3);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('jwt', body.data.jwt);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs in with the account registered above and saves the token as `jwt`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login - wrong password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Bad credentials are rejected in the body', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(false);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Invalid credentials.');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('No token leaks on failure', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.eql(null);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Previous token is left untouched', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('jwt')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"definitely-not-the-password\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same account, wrong password. Same generic message as an unknown email (no user enumeration)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (with JWT)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('User found', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('User found.');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Identity matches the registered account', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.userId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('userId'));",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('userEmail'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Token payload is not exposed', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.not.have.property('passwordHash');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.not.have.property('jwt');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{jwt}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Resolves the bearer token saved by the Login request into the caller's profile."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Me - no token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Security entry point body', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(false);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Authentication required.');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data).to.eql(null);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No Authorization header, which the app expects to answer 401 so it can clear the stored token. Currently returns 500 with Spring's default error body: `/auth/**` is permitAll, so no security entry point runs and the controller gets a null principal (see the collection description). This assertion is the bug signal; it passes once the controller handles a null `userId`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "hunter2",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "jwt",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ]
}
